  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **independent upper-upscale hotel in Mexico**, the main brands an owner should consider for a conversion into a **branded affiliation** are the major **soft-brand / affiliation collections** that let the hotel keep much of its identity while gaining distribution, loyalty, and sales support.[2][5][10][12]\n\nThe strongest candidates from the results are:\n\n- **Marriott**: **Autograph Collection** and **Tribute Portfolio** are specifically positioned as independent-hotel collection brands, with Marriott also noting **The Luxury Collection** as part of its collection-brand offering for independent hotels.[10][13]\n- **Hilton**: **Curio Collection** and **Tapestry Collection** are cited as soft-brand options for independent hotels.[13]\n- **Hyatt**: **The Unbound Collection** and **JdV by Hyatt** are also identified as independent-hotel collection brands.[13]\n- **IHG**: **Vignette Collection** is another soft-brand choice for independent hotels.[13]\n- **Wyndham**: **Registry Collection Hotels** is explicitly described as an **upper-upscale soft brand** for owners seeking brand affiliation while preserving individuality.[1][8]\n- **Choice Hotels**: **Ascend Hotel Collection** is described as a soft brand for independent upscale hotels, including in Mexico.[5][7][9]\n- **Preferred Hotels & Resorts**: not a traditional franchise brand, but a major **independent-hotel affiliation network** in Mexico with collections such as **Legend, L.V.X., Lifestyle, and Connect**.[2][6][17]\n- **SLH (Small Luxury Hotels of the World)** and **WorldHotels**: both are affiliation-style luxury networks that can suit independent upscale properties seeking more flexible brand association.[16][19]\n\nFor a hotel in **Mexico specifically**, two locally relevant options from the results are:\n\n- **Gamma by Posadas**: Posadas offers independent hotels a franchise model where the owner keeps the operation and Posadas supports the property with the **Gamma** brand.[4]\n- **HS HOTSSON / BY HOTSSON / Marca Blanca**: HS HOTSSON offers alternatives for hotels that want to keep their own brand while adopting HS HOTSSON standards and support.[3]\n\nIf you want the **most likely shortlist for an upper-upscale conversion in Mexico**, it would be:\n\n1. **Marriott Autograph Collection / Tribute Portfolio**\n2. **Hilton Curio Collection**\n3. **Hyatt Unbound Collection / JdV by Hyatt**\n4. **Wyndham Registry Collection**\n5. **Choice Ascend Hotel Collection**\n6. **Preferred Hotels & Resorts**\n7. **SLH**\n8. **WorldHotels**\n9. **Gamma by Posadas** for a more Mexico-centric conversion path[1][2][4][7][10][13][16][19]\n\nThe best fit depends on whether the owner wants a **true franchise conversion** with a global chain, or a more flexible **affiliation/soft-brand** model that preserves the hotel’s independent identity.[8][12][13]",
